      "content": "the way you put it makes it sound like his actions were just part of the \"game.\" but if he's literally helping the enemy destroy the city, isn't that eventually just a moral failure regardless of how \"complex\" his motivations were? like, is there actually a way to see his betrayals as anything other than a total lack of principle?",
