    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, i get that, but some historians argue he was basically forced into it because the Athenian democracy was becoming so unstable and paranoid that he couldn't survive there anymore. if the system itself is broken and turning on its own people, can you really call it a \"moral failure\" if someone is just doing what's necessary to avoid being executed? isn't that just realism?",
